@startuml update-ui-state
title Update UI lifecycle (PROPOSED; in-memory only, owned by useAppUpdate)
[*] --> Idle
Idle --> Checking : launch ready / 6 h timer / (none while not Idle)
Checking --> Idle : no update | check error (logged only)
Checking --> Available : newer version
Available --> Dismissed : 나중에
Dismissed --> Checking : 24 h after 나중에 (timer ticks inside the window are skipped)
Available --> Downloading : 지금 업데이트 [UI busy check passes]
Available --> Available : 지금 업데이트 [backend job running] / show reason
Downloading --> Failed : network / signature / disk error
Downloading --> Guarding : download verified
Guarding --> Available : Rust guard Refused (watch or native download active) / show reason, discard bytes
Guarding --> Installing : Allowed -> prepare_for_update (sidecar stopped)
Installing --> Failed : install error (macOS swap failed / NSIS failed)
Installing --> Relaunching : install ok
Relaunching --> [*] : process restart into new version
Failed --> Available : 다시 시도
note right of Failed
  After a failed install the sidecar may be stopped:
  Failed restarts it via the existing backend_restart command
  before showing the retry (old app keeps running).
end note
note bottom of Checking
  Only one check or install in flight (single hook instance).
  Timer cleared on unmount. No state persisted to disk.
end note
@enduml
